    "notationFootnote": "",
    "author": "John Keller",
    "description": "Reproduction study — inspired by Express Stave, Original Version (John Keller, 2005). Same tritone D/G# staff, with DIRECT 7-5 fill (the reverse of the Pianoforte version) — the seven naturals hollow/white, the five black-key notes solid, resembling piano tablature (per the operator reference). This version used the three traditional clefs as register indicators; the middle (alto/C) register is exercised here in register-label (text) mode showing 'C'; the traditional clef glyphs are deferred as assets. The optional B/F centre dash/spot (internal glyph) is an optional identification device and is not rendered (omission). Same continuous-grid D-ledger deviation as the other Express Stave fixtures; half/whole side strokes not in this single-duration preview. Built from the public gallery description/image; not endorsed by or derived from the original.",
